					<div class="chapter-content">
						<p>• Starches and sugars eliminated from&nbsp;the&nbsp;diet.</p>
						<p>• Salivary amylase no longer has long-chain carbohydrates to cleave&nbsp;into&nbsp;glucose.</p>
						<p>• Oral bacteria (Streptococcus mutans) are starved of&nbsp;fermentable&nbsp;substrates.</p>
						<h3>[DAY 3&nbsp;to&nbsp;4]</h3>
						<p>• Bacterial lactic acid production drops&nbsp;toward&nbsp;zero.</p>
						<p>• Gingival sulcus pH rises from an acidic 4.5-5.5 back toward a&nbsp;neutral&nbsp;7.0-7.4.</p>

