					<div class="chapter-content">
						<h3>What Goes on the&nbsp;Safe&nbsp;Plate</h3>
						<p>To keep oral pH strictly neutral and deprive bacteria of fermentable fuel, the baseline diet&nbsp;consists&nbsp;of:</p>
						<p>Ruminant Meats: Ground beef, ribeye steaks, veal, lamb, and organ&nbsp;meats&nbsp;(liver).</p>
						<p>Poultry and Seafood: Chicken, turkey, wild salmon, cod, shrimp, and oysters (which provide natural zinc, copper, and&nbsp;bioavailable&nbsp;B-vitamins).</p>
						<p>Clean Animal Fats: Beef tallow, suet, and natural meat drippings for cooking (avoiding seed and&nbsp;vegetable&nbsp;oils).</p>
						<p>Pasture-Raised Eggs: Boiled, scrambled, or fried in clean&nbsp;animal&nbsp;fat.</p>

					</div>
				</div>

