						<span class="chapter-header-label">Chapter 12: Starving the Fire</span>
						<span class="page-count-label">Page 71</span>
					</div>

					<div class="chapter-content">
						<p>The Single Whole-Food Exception: Fresh whole mushrooms. Mushrooms possess a neutral pH, virtually zero simple sugars, and structural beta-glucans that oral bacteria cannot ferment into&nbsp;lactic&nbsp;acid.</p>
						<p>Hydration: Clean, balanced, mineralized water (testing to ensure it is not unbuffered, acidic RO or distilled water sitting at pH 5.5) and plain&nbsp;mild&nbsp;teas.</p>
						<h3>Seasoning and&nbsp;Sweetener&nbsp;Rules</h3>
						<h3>Many patients inadvertently ruin their elimination baseline by&nbsp;overlooking&nbsp;seasonings:</h3>
						<p>Eliminate: Commercial dry rubs, seasoning blends, and marinades. A close look at ingredient labels reveals hidden citric acid, vinegar powders, dextrose, maltodextrin, and onion/garlic powders - all of which rapidly acidify&nbsp;oral&nbsp;tissues.</p>

					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>71</span>
				</div>
			</section>

