						<p>When applied to bare root dentin, the tin reacts with salivary calcium and phosphate, forming insoluble tin-fluorophosphate mineral crystals that physically precipitate inside the open&nbsp;tubule&nbsp;mouths.</p>
						<p>It acts like microscopic concrete, creating a temporary smear plug that blocks fluid movement and shields pulpal nerves from direct&nbsp;acid&nbsp;contact.</p>

