					<h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 14: The&nbsp;Recovery&nbsp;Protocol</h2>

					<div class="chapter-content is-first-page">
						<p>Even with a strong understanding of your triggers and dental margins,&nbsp;setbacks&nbsp;happen.</p>
						<p>You attend a family wedding and eat a meal seasoned with hidden starches and vinegars. You drink a cup of coffee during a stressful workday. A composite patch at your gumline wears down after years of brushing, quietly exposing root tubules&nbsp;once&nbsp;again.</p>
						<p>When an accidental chemical breach occurs, panic is your worst enemy. You must have an exact, pre-planned protocol to reset the circuit, paired with the psychological mindset to maintain long-term&nbsp;emotional&nbsp;peace.</p>
						<h3>The 6-Day&nbsp;Reset&nbsp;Protocol</h3>
						<p>When you feel the unmistakable smolder of a flare beginning, do not spiral into despair or start throwing random supplements at the pain. Execute a structured&nbsp;6-day&nbsp;reset:</p>
						<h3>Day 1 (The&nbsp;Neutralization&nbsp;Phase):</h3>

					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>79</span>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Chapter 14: The Recovery Protocol (Page 2 of 6) -->
			<section class="book-page" id="page-80">
				<div class="page-body-content">
					<div class="page-running-head">
						<span class="chapter-header-label">Chapter 14: The Recovery Protocol</span>
						<span class="page-count-label">Page 80</span>
					</div>

					<div class="chapter-content">
						<p>Immediately cut all non-baseline foods. Return strictly to plain beef, veal, and&nbsp;clean&nbsp;water.</p>
						<p>Prepare a gentle oral rinse: dissolve half a teaspoon of pure sodium bicarbonate (baking soda) in a cup of lukewarm water. Gently swish and spit after meals to raise oral pH and neutralize lingering&nbsp;surface&nbsp;acids.</p>
						<h3>Days 2 to 3 (The Tubule&nbsp;Shielding&nbsp;Phase):</h3>
						<p>As the 72-hour bacterial fermentation clock peaks, support your&nbsp;exposed&nbsp;margins.</p>
						<p>Apply a small smear of stannous fluoride gel directly to your sensitive root collars before bed, leaving it&nbsp;undisturbed&nbsp;overnight.</p>

					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>80</span>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Chapter 14: The Recovery Protocol (Page 3 of 6) -->
			<section class="book-page" id="page-81">
				<div class="page-body-content">
					<div class="page-running-head">
						<span class="chapter-header-label">Chapter 14: The Recovery Protocol</span>
						<span class="page-count-label">Page 81</span>
					</div>

					<div class="chapter-content">
						<p>Avoid heavy mechanical friction: do not scrub your teeth aggressively with hard bristles; use an ultra-soft toothbrush and gentle,&nbsp;sweeping&nbsp;motions.</p>
						<h3>Days 4 to 6 (The Neurological&nbsp;Settling&nbsp;Phase):</h3>
						<p>With fermentable substrates completely absent, local lactic&nbsp;acid&nbsp;clears.</p>
						<p>ASIC proton channels close, and peripheral action potential&nbsp;frequency&nbsp;declines.</p>
						<p>The Subnucleus Caudalis drains its accumulation of excitatory neurotransmitters, central crosstalk fades, and pain scores settle back&nbsp;toward&nbsp;0/10.</p>

					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>81</span>
				</div>
